body:
Can confirm this on the master branch, I used linux but the issue would be universal as explained in my research here:

This would be a regression from #122510 where a large refactor was made of how this toolbar's buttons work. What's relevant is that the new owner of this logic is `CanvasManipulator ci_manipulator`, and changes to the snap settings must be called through it, it is done properly in "Snap to Parent" this way:

canvas_item_editor_plugin.cpp::3092
```
case SNAP_USE_NODE_PARENT: {
			int snap_mode = ci_manipulator->get_snap_mode() ^ CanvasItemManipulator::SNAP_NODE_PARENT;
			ci_manipulator->set_snap_mode(snap_mode);
			int idx = smartsnap_config_popup->get_item_index(SNAP_USE_NODE_PARENT);
			smartsnap_config_popup->set_item_checked(idx, snap_mode & CanvasItemManipulator::SNAP_NODE_PARENT);
		}
```

Subsequent snap mode cases lack the crucial `ci_manipulator->set_snap_mode(snap_mode);` line, adding them solves the issue, for the most part.

After that fix a new and weird issue appeared, the first time opening the editor would make the selected snap values swallow the first click doing nothing, then working properly after that. It appears there was a problem in how the initial values were loaded, it was using this flawed logic for setting the mode values:

canvas_item_editor_plugin.cpp::3632
```
if (state.has("snap_node_sides")) {
		bool snap_mode = ci_manipulator->get_snap_mode() | (int)state["snap_node_sides"];
		ci_manipulator->set_snap_mode(snap_mode);
		int idx = smartsnap_config_popup->get_item_index(SNAP_USE_NODE_SIDES);
		smartsnap_config_popup->set_item_checked(idx, snap_mode);
	}
```

A typo from the old boolean implementation, it store the modes bitmask into a boolean, losing the actual values, and then using an OR, which cannot turn off a set value. The fix was a simple change from bool to int and allowing the operation to turn off if the value was off: `int snap_mode = (ci_manipulator->get_snap_mode() & ~CanvasItemManipulator::SNAP_NODE_SIDES) | val;`

This would fix the 2D snap toggles. 

However, it experimented with 3D and also found the new 3D snap selectors to be faulty, caused by the migration from the Transform Menu to their own Snap Menu.

<img width="379" height="259" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87d39bf7-e654-42d3-a00a-1059851c6178" />

 Those selectors would do nothing when clicked, except to close unexpectedly the popup menu. It seemed that the issue was simply forgetting to change `transform_menu` to `snap_menu`:

node_3d_editor_plugin.cpp::834
```
case MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_VERTEX: {
			vertex_snap_origin_mode = false;
			int idx_vertex = transform_menu->get_popup()->get_item_index(MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_VERTEX);
			int idx_origin = transform_menu->get_popup()->get_item_index(MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_ORIGIN);
			transform_menu->get_popup()->set_item_checked(idx_vertex, true);
			transform_menu->get_popup()->set_item_checked(idx_origin, false);
		}
```

Now:
```
case MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_VERTEX: {
			vertex_snap_origin_mode = false;
			int idx_vertex = snap_menu->get_popup()->get_item_index(MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_VERTEX);
			int idx_origin = snap_menu->get_popup()->get_item_index(MENU_VERTEX_SNAP_BASE_ORIGIN);
			snap_menu->get_popup()->set_item_checked(idx_vertex, true);
			snap_menu->get_popup()->set_item_checked(idx_origin, false);
		}
```

I will be uploading a PR shortly, the issues are quite simply omissions of the original refactor, so I went ahead and did the code.
